  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 101 PM EST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nSurface high pressure centered over the East Coast continues to \nprovide tranquil, dry weather through Saturday. With increasing WAA \nand dry air in the low levels, temperatures will remain in the mid \n60s for highs tomorrow and Saturday. Highs should be within 5 \ndegrees of the daily record on Friday and Saturday at Fort Wayne and \nSouth Bend!\n\nAs high pressure gets pushed eastward Saturday due to influence from \na trough over the Four Corners region, rain chances return on Sunday \nas a cold front approaches. Chances for rain currently stand at 60-\n80%, however, the day will not be a washout. Scattered, light \nshowers will move through the area at times on Sunday during the \nday. The bulk of the rain looks to move through before the front \ndoes; rainfall amounts are expected to be light as showers should \noutrun the better low level moisture and lift with the actual front. \nIt will be breezy on Sunday with a tightening pressure gradient in \nthe vicinity of the front; Wind gusts will be between 20-25 mph with \na shift in direction from southwest to northwest. \n\nFollowing the frontal passage, CAA and northerly flow ensues with \ntemperatures moderating back towards seasonable levels with highs in \nthe upper 30s to low 40s. The GFS and ECMWF are in solid agreement \nnext week of 850 mb temps as low as -6C to -10C Monday into Tuesday. \nAs a high pressure system spills into the Great Lakes region from \ncentral Canada, the forecast is leaning dry for early into middle \npart of next week. An early preview of Thanksgiving shows dry \nconditions with highs around 40s. Given that a strong El Nino is \nongoing, a more active pattern may develop across the southeastern \nUS with the jet stream keeping activity suppressed to the \nsouth. There is some indication in the long range guidance of a \n'Miller A' type system developing mid to late next week, but a \nlot of uncertainty remains. It is plausible we get a glancing \nblow of some rain/snow showers towards the end of the month, but\nthere are no real signs of winter yet.",
